course: dictionary
lesson: 8955
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around the word, and ask which meaning fits. «The historian Sima Qian wrote that the emperor's tomb has rivers of mercury.» Here Sima is a person's name, because a historian is a person who writes about the past.
explain: Older geography books use sima for a kind of rock. Context is the clue again: if the sentence talks about rock under the oceans, or about continents floating, sima means the rock, not a person. Ask: does this sentence describe a person, or a thing in the Earth?
explain: Check your choice by swapping in your meaning. If you think sima is a person's name, put «a person» in its place and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you are probably right. If it sounds strange, try the other meaning.
fact: Sima has two meanings: a type of rock in geology, and a given name.
fact: Sima (geology, older term) is the lower layer of the Earth's crust, under the oceans and below the continents.
fact: This rock is heavy and rich in silicon and magnesium, which is where the word's parts si and ma come from.
fact: Sima is also a given name in several countries, for example Iran, Croatia and Czechia.
fact: Older books pair sima with «sial», the lighter rock of the continents; modern books usually say «oceanic crust» instead.
exercise: «The historian Sima Qian wrote that the emperor's tomb has rivers of mercury.» In this sentence, what is Sima? | A kind of heavy rock | *A person's name | A tomb in China | A poisonous liquid metal
exercise: Which meaning of sima is about rock? Look for clues about the Earth. | *The lower layer of the Earth's crust, under the oceans | A historian who wrote about emperors | A given name in Croatia | A girl who lives in Czechia
exercise: Ella reads: «Sima is heavy, and it lies below the continents.» What is she reading about? | A person called Sima | *Rock in the Earth | A liquid metal | A tomb
test: «Sima is a common given name, and my cousin is called Sima.» What does sima mean in this sentence? | A poisonous liquid | Heavy rock rich in silicon | A kind of rock under the ocean | *A person's name
test: Why does the word sial appear next to sima in old books? | Sima means lighter rock and sial means heavy rock | Sial and sima are both names of emperors | *Sial is the lighter rock of the continents, and sima is the heavier rock below and under the oceans | Sial means mercury
exam: Maya reads two sentences, «Sima lives in Zagreb» and «Sima is found below the oceans». What is the difference in meaning, and how does context show it? | Both mean the same thing | *The first is a given name and the second is a rock, and the surrounding words show which | Only the second has a meaning | The first is a rock and the second is a name, because Zagreb is a rock
